==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Hot-Footed Frog}}
Hot-Footed Frogs are a type of [[Frog]] that can be located near bodies of [[Water (Terrain)|Water]], either [[Swimming]] or hopping along the bank.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> [[Link]] can [[Crouching|Crouch]] to sneak up and catch them, or alternatively, he can quickly [[Sprinting|Spring]] to capture them before they startle and disappear. Otherwise, Hot-Footed Frogs will run away once they spot him. They can be [[Cooking|Cooked]] alongside [[Monster Part]]s to create [[Hasty Elixir]]s that grant [[Speed Up]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] also accepts them as an ingredient for [[Green Dye]].

A Hot-Footed Frog appears in the ninth [[Recovered Memory]], "[[Silent Princess (Memory)|Silent Princess]]", wherein [[Zelda]] captures one to show Link.<ref name="BotW Zelda"/> She excitedly shares that it is a delicacy known to have potent effects.<ref name="BotW Zelda 2"/> She then states that [[Hyrule Castle]]'s research shows that eating one can enhance certain abilities, going on to add that while they are not in a controlled environment, Link's high level of physical fitness would make him perfect for the study.<ref name="BotW Zelda 3"/> She presses him to taste it,<ref name="BotW Zelda 4"/> to which Link reacts poorly.

Hot-Footed Frogs are required to [[Enhancing|Enhance]] the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Hot-Footed Frog}}

